    "id": "skool-vault-the-difference-between-people-who-ship-and-people-who-keep-setting-up",
    "section": "vault",
    "platform": "skool",
    "status": "Idea",
    "title": "The Difference Between People Who Ship and People Who Keep “Setting Up”",
    "post": "I've been noticing something while watching people in this community.\n\nSome people consistently ship things, while others are still stuck in the “setting up” phase.\n\nAnd honestly, the difference usually isn't the AI model they're using. It's not the number of MCPs they have installed, and it's not even their CLAUDE.md.\n\nThe biggest difference I've noticed is one simple habit:\n\nPeople who ship consistently know what they want the final output to look like before they start the session.\n\nNot just the task. The actual output.\n\nBefore opening Claude Code, try answering these three questions in one paragraph:\n\n- What should the finished product look like when someone opens it in their browser?\n- What should the visitor be able to do when they land on it?\n- What does success look like specifically, rather than vaguely?\n\nI've noticed that when you can't clearly answer these questions before starting, you often spend a large part of the session correcting the direction. You're not really building yet—you’re going back and forth with Claude, trying to figure out what you actually want.\n\nBut when you have a clear picture of the output from the beginning, the first result is usually much closer to what you had in mind. Then, instead of constantly changing direction, you can spend the rest of the session refining and improving.\n\nTo me, that's one of the biggest differences between fast builders and slow builders. It's not always about technical skill. A lot of the time, it's simply clarity.\n\nTry this before your next Claude Code session: write down the answers to those three questions in your notes app before you start. Then include them as context in your first prompt.\n\nYou might be surprised by how much closer your first version gets to what you actually wanted.\n\nHow clear and specific is your brief before you start building? 👇",
    "note": "Selected from Claude Codex Mastery for strong engagement and a useful comment discussion.",
    "source": "Claude Codex Mastery",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.skool.com/yar-ai-automation-school-9911/the-difference-between-people-who-ship-and-people-who-keep-setting-up",
